from the market. In the United States, the DEA and comparable state-level agencies also heavily regulate the manufacturing, holding, processing, security,
recordkeeping and distribution of drugs that are considered controlled substances, and the DEA periodically inspects facilities for compliance with its rules
and regulations.
Our ability to generate revenues from any of our drugs that receive regulatory approval will be subject to a variety of risks, many of which are out of
our control.
Any drug that may be approved for marketing may not gain market acceptance among patients, healthcare providers, healthcare payers or the medical
community. We believe that the degree of market acceptance and our ability to generate revenues from such products will depend on a number of factors,
